{=============================================================================
  Air-source heat pump with R410A (evaporator air side, water condenser)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0054
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  An air-to-water heat pump runs on R410A: the evaporator draws heat from the
  outdoor air (15 K air cooling, pressure drop of 0.32 bar), the condenser
  heats a water circuit (e.g. floor heating). The model determines the
  refrigerant flow rate from the condenser heat balance, the evaporator air
  flow rate from the evaporator heat balance, and the compressor isentropic
  efficiency. R410A is zeotropic: under the dome the temperature at a given
  pressure also depends on the quality, so state temperatures are obtained
  from (P, h) or (P, x), never from T_sat alone (as in the original).
  Cycle states: 1 compressor inlet / evaporator outlet (saturated vapour),
  2 condenser inlet, 3 condenser outlet, 4 evaporator inlet (after the
  isenthalpic expansion valve).

  Inputs : p_su_ev, DP_ev, T_su_cd, p_su_cd, T_ex_cd, m_dot_w_cool,
           DELTAT_w, DELTAT_air, fluid$
  Outputs: m_dot_R410a, m_dot_air, COP, eta_is_cp (and the state points
           p[i], T[i], h[i], s[i], i = 1..4)
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège, course "Thermodynamique appliquée" (MECA0002), repetition 8,
           exercise 2, 2022-2023 (EES file R08_E02_2022.EES) - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"!Data"
fluid$ = 'R410A'
p_su_ev = 800E3 [Pa]        "evaporator inlet pressure (800 kPa in the original)"
DP_ev = 32000 [Pa]          "evaporator pressure drop (0.32*1e2 kPa in the original)"
T_su_cd = 105 [°C]          "condenser inlet temperature"
p_su_cd = 3000E3 [Pa]       "condenser inlet pressure (3000 kPa in the original)"
T_ex_cd = 45 [°C]           "condenser outlet temperature"
m_dot_w_cool = 0.1 [kg/s]   "cooling-water flow rate"
DELTAT_w = 25 [°C]          "water temperature rise"
DELTAT_air = -15 [°C]       "air cooling (negative by convention)"

"!Solution"

"The useful effect of the heat pump is the heat given by the working fluid to the
water loop at the condenser; the condenser is a refrigerant - water exchanger whose
water circuit can feed a floor heating system, as in the original."

"The heat is extracted from the outside air at the evaporator: a refrigerant - air
exchanger in which the air gives heat to the working fluid, as in the original."

"Condenser analysis. Index 1 is used for the compressor inlet. The heat pump
comprises, in order: 1. compressor, 2. condenser, 3. expansion valve, 4. evaporator."
T[2] = T_su_cd
p[2] = p_su_cd
h[2] = enthalpy(fluid$, p=p[2], T=T[2])
s[2] = entropy(fluid$, p=p[2], T=T[2])
x_2 = quality(fluid$, h=h[2], p=p[2])       "state 2: superheated vapour at the condenser inlet"

T[3] = T_ex_cd
p[3] = p[2]                                 "pressure drop neglected in the condenser (as specified in the statement)"
h[3] = enthalpy(fluid$, p=p[3], T=T[3])
s[3] = entropy(fluid$, p=p[3], T=T[3])
x_3 = quality(fluid$, h=h[3], p=p[3])       "state 3: subcooled liquid at the condenser outlet"

Q_dot_cd = m_dot_R410a*(h[3] - h[2])        "heat lost by the R410A in the condenser -> negative"
Q_dot_w = m_dot_w_cool*c_w*DELTAT_w         "heat taken by the water of the secondary circuit"
c_w = 4187 [J/kg-K]                         "specific heat of liquid water (4.187 kJ/kg-K in the original)"

Q_dot_cd + Q_dot_w = 0                      "condenser heat balance: what the R410A gives up is
                                            recovered by the water; gives the R410A flow rate"

"Evaporator analysis"
p[4] = p_su_ev
h[4] = h[3]                                 "isenthalpic expansion valve (open system, no work, adiabatic)"
T[4] = temperature(fluid$, h=h[4], p=p[4])
s[4] = entropy(fluid$, h=h[4], p=p[4])
x_4 = quality(fluid$, h=h[4], p=p[4])

p[1] = p[4] - DP_ev                         "pressure drop in the evaporator"
x_1 = 1
"No superheat being specified, the fluid leaves as saturated vapour at p = p[1]
(as in the original): the compressor cannot admit liquid."

h[1] = enthalpy(fluid$, p=p[1], x=x_1)
s[1] = entropy(fluid$, p=p[1], x=x_1)
T[1] = temperature(fluid$, p=p[1], x=x_1)   "T_sat is not used here because R410A is zeotropic:
                                            under the dome T depends on the quality, not on P alone
                                            (as in the original)"

Q_dot_ev = m_dot_R410a*(h[1] - h[4])        "heat taken by the R410A in the evaporator, positive"
Q_dot_air = m_dot_air*c_air*DELTAT_air      "heat given by the air -> negative (DELTAT_air < 0)"
c_air = 1005 [J/kg-K]                       "specific heat of air at ambient T and p, course value
                                            (1.005 kJ/kg-K in the original)"
Q_dot_ev + Q_dot_air = 0                    "evaporator heat balance: gives the air flow rate"

"Compressor analysis"
W_dot_cmp = m_dot_R410a*(h[2] - h[1])       "power required by the compressor, positive"
COP = -Q_dot_cd/W_dot_cmp                   "COP = useful effect / costly effect"

h_2_is = enthalpy(fluid$, p=p[2], s=s[1])
eta_is_cp = (h_2_is - h[1])/(h[2] - h[1])
